# Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and you're ready to run: `pnpm install && pnpm dev`.
#
# ── Assets ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The compiled game content (track/bike/prop GLBs, textures, the soundtrack)
# is NOT in this repository — it's ~hundreds of MB of binaries served from a
# public CDN instead. Point the app at that CDN and it streams everything at
# runtime; nothing to download, and you always get the current build.
#
# This is all a fresh clone needs. Without it the app boots to "Boot failed",
# because it looks for assets under the local `public/` directory that isn't
# populated.
VITE_ASSET_BASE_URL=https://hoverbike-content.mattscott.dev

# Maintainers with bucket credentials can instead hydrate a local copy with
# `pnpm assets:pull` (rclone + an R2 token) and leave this unset — useful for
# working offline or re-exporting assets. See docs/asset-storage.md.

# ── Leaderboard (optional, maintainer-only) ───────────────────────────────
# Signs Time-Trial submissions to the global board. Must match the deployed
# PartyKit project's LEADERBOARD_HMAC_SECRET. Unset is fine for local dev and
# for contributors: it falls through to a well-known dev value, and the local
# leaderboard cache works regardless.
# VITE_LEADERBOARD_HMAC_SECRET=
